   "text": {
    "L1": "Turn symmetry means a shape looks exactly the same after a turn before one full turn.",
    "L2": "A full turn does not count, because every shape matches itself then.",
    "L3": "Count the matches in one full turn. A square matches four times, while a three-blade fan matches three times.",
    "L4": "The smallest matching turn is one full turn divided by the number of matches.",
    "L5": "So a square matches after a quarter turn, and a three-blade fan after one-third of a turn.",
    "L6": "Here is a useful contrast: S has turn symmetry but no mirror line.",
    "L7": "A has a mirror line but no turn symmetry. These are different ideas.",
    "L8": "Now check the fan by counting its matches in one full turn."
   },
